      "content": "Grief of this magnitude often requires professional intervention that goes beyond standard advice, especially when it feels as absolute as the loss of one's core identity. Since you feel so disconnected from who you were, it is crucial to speak to a therapist or crisis line who understands that rebuilding isn't about memorizing old roles but finding a new, living way to exist. You are not gone, even when it feels incredibly painful to believe otherwise; reaching out for immediate support could be the only bridge between this void and any chance of feeling human again.",
